  :adr/body "# closing 2026-08-19/20 — the same defect in nine places, and two predictions I got wrong\n\nOne shape ran through the whole session: **a check that could not run returns\nwhat a check that ran and found nothing returns.** It is not a bug that\nappears once and is fixed; it is a shape that reappears one layer up every\ntime the previous instance is closed.\n\n## Where it appeared today\n\n| where | what it looked like |\n|---|---|\n| fleet gate addressing | `root-source-nul-bytes` had no `:org`, so west resolved `root` to **etzhayyim/root**. Thirteen receipts, none at a commit in this repository |\n| sparse cone | `verify-valueflows-binding` reported five `high` findings because its five inputs are outside the checkout cone. All five are in `origin/main` |\n| stale checkouts | 20 NUL findings; **13 were already fixed on their repo main**, reported from checkouts behind by 2 to 324 commits |\n| ADR ids | seven collisions in four days, an eighth an hour after fixing them, three more five hours later |\n| reflection surface | thirteen gated repos with nowhere to report a failure, and the set grew three times in one day while being edited |\n| maturity plane | `repo-taxonomy` 17 days stale, and — the real one — the scan follows `:local/root` only |\n| docs truncation | one unescaped quote swallowed half an ADR body. The file **parses** |\n\n## Two predictions I got wrong, both recorded rather than quietly corrected\n\n1. **\"Fixing the taxonomy will bring the 400 unmeasured repos in.\"** It did\n   not. Count was 1,938 before and after. The real reason is\n   `itonami-maturity-scan.cljs:135` — the scan follows `:local/root` edges\n   and nothing else, so `worklaw` is measured (sibling path) and `taxlaw` is\n   not (git dep). **The design choice that makes a repo forkable removes it\n   from the maturity plane.** Widening the scan is a decision about what this\n   plane measures, not a bug fix, so it is named and not done.\n\n2. **\"There are two findings in adr-identity.\"** There were eight. I read\n   `tail -8` of the output and reported the tail as the whole. The same\n   mis-measurement appeared four times today in different clothes: `$?` read\n   through a pipe (four times), `max` applied to strings, `set -- $p` not\n   splitting in zsh (five times), and a regex sweep that answered 221 where\n   the EDN reader answers 224.\n\n## What is now true\n\nFour fleet gates green that were not: `root-repository-roles` 21/0,\n`root-adr-identity` 20/0, `root-reflection-surface` 21/0,\n`root-source-nul-bytes` 21/0. `root-docs-edn-truncation` back to green.\n\nThe orgs-detector scheduler is installed and has run two automatic passes.\nA full pass is **14m10s**; the 402-minute figure I worried about was a sum of\ntimeout ceilings, which is not a duration.\n\nThe NUL plane is clean: two real bytes fixed, and the remaining 14 findings\nare `info`/`stale-checkout` — the detector now asks git whether the byte is\nin what the repo publishes before calling it a defect.\n\n`kotoba-lang/taxlaw` gained 申告 (法人税法 第七十四条, 所得税法 第百二十条) and\n真実性 (電帳法施行規則 第四条第一項), and `cloud-itonami-isco-4311` gained the\ntwo consumers. Neither computes a tax figure, and both say why in the\nstatute's own words. isco-4311 moved 0.2883 to 0.5008 as a side effect.\n\n## Resume points, stated as checks rather than claims\n\n- **The `:local/root` scope of the maturity scan is an owner decision.**\n  Widening it to git deps pulls in a large number of repos and moves every\n  number in the dataset.\n- **1,696 orgs-detector findings, of which eleven detectors are still first-run\n  baselines.** Nobody has triaged them. The first pass that can say NEW or\n  RESOLVED for those has now happened for some; the rest follow their own\n  intervals.\n- **`aiueos/audit.cljc`** — TCB inventory fail-closed on\n  `:external-undeclared`. Expanding the TCB is the owner's call.\n- **`cofog` will not generate a west entry.** Six hypotheses eliminated and\n  recorded in ADR-2608197200; the seventh needs a debug print inside the\n  generator.\n- **The ADR id hook is new and unproven in the wild.** It denied correctly in\n  six exercised cases, but no other session has hit it yet. If it turns out to\n  block something legitimate, the fix is to narrow `bare-id`, not to remove\n  the guard.\n\n## Owner WIP left untouched\n\n`90-docs/adr/2608011100-m365-...edn` has an uncommitted addition dated today\n(Mail.Send.Shared tenant grant). Not mine; not touched.\n"}]
